====================================================================================================
PART 3 -- THE CONSEQUENCE: the two-phase architecture's cluster-side PHASE DIAGRAM (fit numbers)
====================================================================================================
  PHASE 1 -- the PHANTOM phase (equilibration exists): M500 > M_sat = 3.09e+14 Msun
      f_dust(M500) = 0.674 (M500/8e14)^(-0.414) -- the phantom coexists with the dust;
      measured on the 12 X-COP clusters (G098 floor-A medians on [0.2,1] R500): per-cluster f_dust =
      A1644 0.70, RXC1825 0.75, A3158 0.69, A1795 0.66, A2255 0.67, A85 0.64, A644 0.84, A2319 0.60, ZW1215 0.70, A3266 0.52, A2029 0.67, A2142 0.56
      (range 0.52-0.84; sample median 0.674 at the pivot) -> phantom share 1-f_dust = 0.16-0.48
      the dust's share FALLS with mass (q < 0): f_dust(3.5e14) ~ 0.95, f_dust(8e14) = 0.67, f_dust(9e14) ~ 0.64; the large clusters carry LESS dust per unit missing mass
  PHASE 2 -- the ALL-DUST phase (equilibration oscillates out): M500 < M_sat
      f_dust = 1.0 (SATURATED: the whole missing mass is dust, the phantom's share -> 0);
      the 26 E11 groups (M500 = 5.20e+12-1.73e+14) ALL sit in this phase;
      this lane's test: implied f_dust median 0.919 (dev -0.081 = the baryon floor), vs the cluster-side median 0.674 -- the phase contrast 1.36x
  THE BOUNDARY -- M_sat = 3.088e+14 Msun (band [1.730e+14, 4.010e+14] from q +- 0.16)
      sits in a 0.30-dex DATA GAP: most massive group IC1633 = 1.73e14, least massive cluster A1644 = 3.48e14;
      NOTHING is measured in [1.73e14, 3.48e14] -- the boundary's location is DERIVED from the fit, the two regimes are MEASURED at their endpoints.
  THE CONSEQUENCE STATEMENT: the phantom's galactic-scale equilibrated sector (M_ph = M_b at r_M =
      sqrt(G M_b/a0), the MW-anchored equipartition) OSCILLATES OUT at group scale: at r_M ~ 0.13 R500 the
      linear phantom would already claim the baryon mass, and extended to R500 it would claim (R500/r_M) f_b ~ 7.7 x 0.08 ~ 0.63 of the total -- the EQUILIBRIUM (the two-phase coexistence) EXISTS ONLY ABOVE
      ~3e14, in the tail of the mass function; below it the missing mass is all dust, and the group sample is
      the phase diagram's first all-dust measurement.

====================================================================================================
V -- THE VERDICTS
====================================================================================================
  [PASS] V1 [the groups' implied f_dust vs 1.0]
         measured: median 0.919, dev -0.081, range [0.882, 0.967]
         reading : THE GROUPS' IMPLIED f_dust vs 1.0 (THE DEVIATION): the 26 E11 groups (M500 = 5.2e+12-1.7e+14, ALL below M_sat = 3.09e+14) imply, through the equipartition inversion M_ph(<R500) = M_b -> dust share = 1 - M_b/M500, a median f_dust = 0.919 (mean 0.924, inv-var 0.951; per-group range [0.882, 0.967], std 0.029) vs the saturation prediction 1.0 -- DEVIATION -0.081 (-8.1% below saturation).  The deviation is EXACTLY the baryon floor: f_dust = 1 - f_b with median f_b = 0.081 (f_gas,500 median 0.061 + 0.02 stars) -- i.e. the phantom's maximal equilibrated share at group scale is 8.1% of the total (8.8% of the missing mass in the strict reading), versus 26-48% measured share on the clusters (G098 median phantom share 0.33).  The strict missing-mass variant gives 0.912 (dev -0.088); the LINEAR-LAW anti-branch (phantom = M_b R500/r_M, no saturation) would demand 0.34 (cluster-like) and is REJECTED by the measured group rise +0.536 and the a_c ~ 1.4-5.8 amplitude run.  VERDICT: the groups sit AT SATURATION up to the 8% baryon-floor correction -- the missing mass below 3e14 is ~92-100% dust, the phantom's share <= ~8-9% (the equipartition ceiling), vs ~30-40% typical on the clusters: the saturation prediction f_dust ~ 1 is CONFIRMED to within the floor's residual.
  [PASS] V2 [the phase diagram's reality]
         measured: clusters 0.52-0.84 (n=12, phantom present); groups implied 0.92+-0.03 (n=26, all-dust); boundary M_sat = 3.09e+14 DERIVED (0.30-dex gap)
         reading : THE PHASE DIAGRAM'S REALITY: the two regimes ARE measured at their endpoints -- the phantom phase on the 12 clusters (M500 = 3.48-8.95e14, f_dust medians 0.52-0.84, phantom share up to 0.48) and the all-dust phase on the 26 groups (M500 = 5.2e12-1.73e14, implied f_dust 0.92+-0.03) -- but the BOUNDARY itself at M_sat = 3.09e+14 (band [1.7e+14, 4.0e+14]) is DERIVED from the fit (f_ref x the q run), NOT measured: nothing sits in the 0.30-dex gap between IC1633 (1.73e14) and A1644 (3.48e14).  The nearest-to-boundary cluster A1644 (3.48e14, 1.13x M_sat) measures a phantom share of 0.30 -- the phantom EXISTS just above the boundary -- while the groups' maximal share is 0.08: the contrast across the boundary is in the phase diagram's direction, but a sharp transition at 3.09e14 is an extrapolation, and the phase diagram is REAL as a two-regime statement with its boundary location still unmeasured.
  [PASS] V3 [the honest statement -- a falsifiable prediction with the group sample as its first test]
         measured: implied 0.919 vs 1.0 (dev -0.081); falsifier: f_dust < 0.85 measured on any group or gap system
         reading : HONEST: the sub-3e14 universe is ALL DUST -- a falsifiable prediction (G140's saturation bound made concrete here): the first test, the 26-group sample, returns implied f_dust median 0.919 = 1.0 - f_b (deviation -0.081, the baryon floor) -- CONSISTENT with saturation, within the floor's residual and at 1.36x the cluster-side median 0.674; the falsifier is registered: ANY group with a measured dust share of the missing mass well below ~0.85 (a resolved group-scale a_c from T(r) profiles, or a system in the [1.73, 3.48]e14 gap showing f_dust < 0.85) voids the all-dust phase; the boundary's measured location (the gap-filling system) and the group T(r) extraction (G140's C1, not executable on the committed record) are the two open measurements; the group data remain UNVERIFIED-in-repo (G143's transcription, gated vs G125), and the deviation's systematic character (it is the baryon floor, not scatter) is stated rather than buried.

